# NOTICE

This repository contains third-party market and economic data, committed under
`data/vendor_payloads/` so that the research here can be reproduced from a clean checkout.
The data is included for that purpose only. It is not original to this project, and
publishing it here does not transfer or alter anyone's rights in it.

## Provenance of the committed payloads

| Payload tree | Source | Rights |
|---|---|---|
| `data/vendor_payloads/nasdaq_bars/` | Nasdaq historical quote service (`api.nasdaq.com`) | The data remains Nasdaq's. Included as served, unmodified. |
| `data/vendor_payloads/nasdaq_dividends/` | Nasdaq dividend history (`api.nasdaq.com`) | The data remains Nasdaq's. Included as served, unmodified. |
| `data/vendor_payloads/cboe_vix/` | Cboe Global Markets published index history (`cdn.cboe.com`) | The data remains Cboe's. Cboe publishes these CSV files openly. |
| `data/vendor_payloads/fred/` | Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis, FRED (`fred.stlouisfed.org`) | Series produced by US government bodies are in the public domain; series redistributed by FRED from other providers remain those providers'. |

Each file is the untouched HTTP response body as received, gzip-compressed, named by the
instant it was fetched. Nothing in these trees has been edited, reformatted or corrected;
every transformation this project applies happens downstream, in the curated tier, which is
**not** committed.

## Why the payloads are here at all

The Nasdaq endpoint serves only a trailing ten-year window. Sessions that fall out of that
window cannot be fetched again at any price, so a repository holding only the download scripts
would, after a year, be unable to reproduce its own results. Committing the payloads is what
makes the dataset reproducible rather than merely described. The reasoning, the alternatives
considered, and the fact that this knowingly departs from the project's own preference for
publishing code and derived metrics rather than raw vendor data, are recorded in
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-20-phase1-data-and-targets-design.md`, section 13.

## If you are a rights holder

If you are one of the sources above and would prefer your data not be redistributed here,
open an issue or contact the repository owner and it will be removed from the working tree and
from git history.

